---
import '../styles/global.css';
import { nav } from '../layouts';

const technologies = ['Python', 'TDD', 'BDD', 'CI/CD', 'IaC', 'Kafka', 'RabbitMQ'];
const optionalTechnologies = ['AWS', 'Kubernetes', 'Terraform', 'Databricks', 'Airflow', 'Kubeflow'];
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff" />
    <meta name="description" content="Task 2: responsive UX/UI redesign of a Prima Software Engineering vacancy." />
    <title>Task 2 | Make something better</title>
  </head>
  <body class="task2-page">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="shell header-inner">
        <a class="wordmark" href="/prima-employer-brand-takehome/">PRIMA</a>
        <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
          {nav.map((item) => <a href={`/prima-employer-brand-takehome${item.href}`} aria-current={item.href === '/task-2/' ? 'page' : undefined}>{item.label}</a>)}
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="task-hero">
        <div class="shell task-head">
          <div class="task-number"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Make something better</span></div>
          <h1>Turn a job ad into a decision tool.</h1>
          <p class="lead">I selected a real Prima vacancy and redesigned the desktop experience around the questions a candidate needs to answer before applying. The mobile view then adapts the same logic for smaller screens.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="shell asset-intro">
          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">Asset selected</div>
            <h2 style="margin-top:10px">Senior Python Software Engineer</h2>
            <p class="lead asset-lead">Prima Careers · Milan · Engineering</p>
          </div>
          <div class="asset-meta-card">
            <span>Permanent</span>
            <span>Full remote available</span>
            <span>€40k–€75k</span>
            <span>ML Platform Domain</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section task2-section">
        <div class="shell">
          <div class="stage-heading">
            <div>
              <div class="eyebrow">01 / Before</div>
              <h2>The current vacancy, mapped as a desktop journey.</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="small">A structured reconstruction of the published vacancy hierarchy. The page is not presented as a pixel-perfect screenshot.</p>
          </div>

          <article class="browser-frame browser-before">
            <div class="browser-chrome">
              <div class="browser-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
              <div class="browser-url">helloprima.com / careers / senior-python-software-engineer</div>
              <div class="browser-label">DESKTOP</div>
            </div>
            <div class="job-current-hero">
              <div class="current-hero-grid">
                <div>
                  <div class="job-label">Senior Python Software Engineer</div>
                  <h3>Are you looking for a new challenge?</h3>
                  <p>Fancy helping us shape the future of motor insurance?</p>
                </div>
                <div class="current-facts-panel">
                  <div class="job-facts"><span>Milan</span><span>Permanent</span><span>Full remote available</span><span>€40k–€75k</span></div>
                  <a class="current-apply-note" href="https://www.helloprima.com/careers/jobs/senior-python-software-engineer-77dc9214-4ed8-470e-93b0-4de8bbb1ccc4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><b>Apply now ↗</b></a>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="current-desktop-body">
              <aside class="current-sidebar">
                <div class="section-kicker">Current journey</div>
                <div class="current-nav-item">01 <span>Prima</span></div>
                <div class="current-nav-item">02 <span>Engineering</span></div>
                <div class="current-nav-item">03 <span>ML Platform Domain</span></div>
                <div class="current-nav-item">04 <span>Role & requirements</span></div>
                <div class="current-nav-item">05 <span>Why you'll love it here</span></div>
              </aside>

              <div class="current-main">
                <section>
                  <div class="section-kicker">01 / Prima</div>
                  <h4>Company story and broader context</h4>
                  <p>The candidate gets the wider company context before reaching the distinctive value proposition of the role.</p>
                </section>
                <section>
                  <div class="section-kicker">02 / Engineering</div>
                  <h4>Wider Engineering context</h4>
                  <p>Useful context about the function appears before the more specific ML Platform opportunity.</p>
                </section>
                <section class="current-highlight">
                  <div class="section-kicker">03 / ML Platform Domain</div>
                  <h4>Foundational platforms for Machine Learning at scale</h4>
                  <p>This is one of the strongest reasons to care about the role, but it arrives after broader context.</p>
                </section>
                <section>
                  <div class="section-kicker">04 / Role & requirements</div>
                  <h4>Responsibilities, requirements and nice-to-haves</h4>
                  <p>The detailed job information is useful and specific, but the decision context could be surfaced earlier.</p>
                </section>
                <section>
                  <div class="section-kicker">05 / Why you'll love it here</div>
                  <h4>Work Your Way · Grow with us · Thrive and perform</h4>
                  <p>EVP content and broader benefits appear toward the end of the page.</p>
                </section>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="shell">
          <div class="stage-heading">
            <div>
              <div class="eyebrow">02 / What’s wrong</div>
              <h2>Not a content problem. A usability and hierarchy problem.</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="small">The vacancy already contains strong information. The opportunity is to make the information architecture work harder for a candidate who is scanning, comparing and deciding.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="friction-grid friction-grid-3">
            <article class="friction-card">
              <span class="friction-number">01</span>
              <h3>Priority information comes late</h3>
              <p>The ML Platform context is distinctive, but the candidate reaches it after broader company and Engineering context.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="friction-card">
              <span class="friction-number">02</span>
              <h3>Impact is harder to scan</h3>
              <p>Responsibilities are present, but the relationship between the work, the problems and the impact is not as immediate as it could be.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="friction-card">
              <span class="friction-number">03</span>
              <h3>Candidate questions are mixed</h3>
              <p>What would I do? Who would I work with? How could I grow? What happens next? The answers exist, but the hierarchy can make them harder to retrieve.</p>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="usability-strip">
            <div><span class="usability-icon">A</span><div><strong>Scannability</strong><small>Short blocks, clear headings, visible hierarchy.</small></div></div>
            <div><span class="usability-icon">B</span><div><strong>Orientation</strong><small>Section navigation shows where the candidate is.</small></div></div>
            <div><span class="usability-icon">C</span><div><strong>Action</strong><small>The apply action stays available without dominating the page.</small></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section after-stage">
        <div class="shell">
          <div class="stage-heading">
            <div>
              <div class="eyebrow">03 / After</div>
              <h2>A desktop redesign, with a deliberate mobile adaptation.</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="small">The desktop view is the primary design. The mobile view below shows how the same content model changes when space, navigation and thumb reach become constraints.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="responsive-previews">
            <article class="preview-panel desktop-preview">
              <div class="preview-panel-head">
                <div><span class="preview-kicker">PRIMARY UI</span><h3>Desktop</h3></div>
                <span class="preview-device">1440px layout</span>
              </div>

              <div class="browser-frame browser-after">
                <div class="browser-chrome">
                  <div class="browser-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                  <div class="browser-url">helloprima.com / careers / senior-python-software-engineer</div>
                  <div class="browser-label">DESKTOP</div>
                </div>

                <div class="after-hero">
                  <div class="after-crumb">Engineering / Machine Learning Platform</div>
                  <div class="after-hero-grid">
                    <div>
                      <div class="after-eyebrow">Senior Python Software Engineer</div>
                      <h3>Build the platforms that enable Machine Learning at scale at Prima.</h3>
                      <p class="after-intro">Join the ML Platform Domain and help build foundational platforms that support Machine Learning across Prima’s markets, from experimentation to production.</p>
                      <div class="after-facts"><span>Milan</span><span>Permanent</span><span>Full remote</span><span>€40k–€75k</span></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="after-apply">
                      <span>Ready to explore the role?</span>
                      <a href="https://www.helloprima.com/careers/jobs/senior-python-software-engineer-77dc9214-4ed8-470e-93b0-4de8bbb1ccc4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Apply now ↗</a>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="redesign-shell">
                  <aside class="after-nav" aria-label="Role page sections">
                    <a href="#impact">Impact</a>
                    <a href="#work">Work</a>
                    <a href="#team">Team</a>
                    <a href="#tech">Tech</a>
                    <a href="#growth">Growth</a>
                    <a href="#hiring">Hiring</a>
                    <a href="#why-prima">Why Prima</a>
                  </aside>

                  <div class="desktop-role-layout">
                    <div class="redesign-content">
                      <section id="impact" class="redesign-block">
                        <div class="section-kicker">01 / Your impact</div>
                        <h4>Help build the platform behind ML at scale.</h4>
                        <div class="impact-grid">
                          <div><b>Scale</b><span>Shared capabilities for Machine Learning across Prima’s markets.</span></div>
                          <div><b>Lifecycle</b><span>Systems supporting experimentation, training, deployment and monitoring.</span></div>
                          <div><b>Collaboration</b><span>Work with Product Managers, Data Scientists, ML Engineers and other technical stakeholders.</span></div>
                        </div>
                      </section>

                      <section id="work" class="redesign-block">
                        <div class="section-kicker">02 / What you’ll work on</div>
                        <div class="role-list">
                          <div><span>01</span><b>Build platform capabilities</b><p>Platform tools, shared services and infrastructure for ML at scale.</p></div>
                          <div><span>02</span><b>Support the ML lifecycle</b><p>Systems supporting experimentation, training, deployment and monitoring.</p></div>
                          <div><span>03</span><b>Solve complex engineering problems</b><p>Reliable, maintainable software with a strong focus on quality and scalability.</p></div>
                          <div><span>04</span><b>Share expertise</b><p>Technical guidance, mentorship and support within the ML Platform Domain.</p></div>
                        </div>
                      </section>

                      <section id="team" class="redesign-block split-block">
                        <div><div class="section-kicker">03 / Your team</div><h4>Work at the intersection of engineering, ML and product.</h4></div>
                        <div class="team-tags"><span>Product Managers</span><span>Data Scientists</span><span>ML Engineers</span><span>Software Engineers</span></div>
                      </section>

                      <section id="tech" class="redesign-block">
                        <div class="section-kicker">04 / Your engineering environment</div>
                        <div class="tech-row">{technologies.map(t => <span>{t}</span>)}</div>
                        <p class="small">Additional technologies are shown as relevant possibilities, not assumed day-to-day requirements.</p>
                        <div class="tech-row optional">{optionalTechnologies.map(t => <span>{t}</span>)}</div>
                      </section>

                      <section id="growth" class="redesign-block split-block">
                        <div><div class="section-kicker">05 / Your growth</div><h4>See how Prima supports development once you join.</h4></div>
                        <div class="growth-list"><span>Learning resources</span><span>Mentorship</span><span>A growth plan tailored to you</span></div>
                      </section>

                      <section id="hiring" class="redesign-block split-block">
                        <div><div class="section-kicker">06 / What to expect</div><h4>Make the next step visible before you apply.</h4></div>
                        <div><p>Bring the relevant hiring information closer to the vacancy without duplicating the full company-wide process.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.helloprima.com/careers/jobs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">See the hiring process ↗</a></div>
                      </section>

                      <section id="why-prima" class="redesign-block why-prima-block">
                        <div class="section-kicker">07 / Why Prima</div>
                        <div class="evp-row"><b>Work Your Way</b><b>Grow with us</b><b>Thrive and perform</b></div>
                        <div class="final-apply"><div><strong>Ready to build what’s next?</strong><span>See the role in full and apply when you’re ready.</span></div><a href="https://www.helloprima.com/careers/jobs/senior-python-software-engineer-77dc9214-4ed8-470e-93b0-4de8bbb1ccc4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Apply now ↗</a></div>
                      </section>
                    </div>

                    <aside class="desktop-rail">
                      <div class="rail-card rail-sticky">
                        <div class="section-kicker">Role at a glance</div>
                        <div class="rail-fact"><b>Team</b><span>ML Platform Domain</span></div>
                        <div class="rail-fact"><b>Location</b><span>Milan · Full remote available</span></div>
                        <div class="rail-fact"><b>Level</b><span>Senior</span></div>
                        <div class="rail-fact"><b>Salary</b><span>€40k–€75k</span></div>
                        <a class="rail-apply" href="https://www.helloprima.com/careers/jobs/senior-python-software-engineer-77dc9214-4ed8-470e-93b0-4de8bbb1ccc4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Apply now ↗</a>
                      </div>
                    </aside>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="preview-panel mobile-preview">
              <div class="preview-panel-head">
                <div><span class="preview-kicker">RESPONSIVE ADAPTATION</span><h3>Mobile</h3></div>
                <span class="preview-device">390px viewport</span>
              </div>

              <div class="phone-shell">
                <div class="phone">
                  <div class="phone-bar"></div>
                  <div class="phone-hero">
                    <div class="phone-kicker">Senior Python Software Engineer</div>
                    <div class="phone-title">Build the platforms behind ML at scale.</div>
                    <div class="phone-sub">ML Platform Domain · Prima</div>
                    <div class="phone-meta"><span>Milan</span><span>Full remote</span><span>€40k–€75k</span></div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="phone-mobile-nav">
                    <a href="#mobile-impact">Impact</a><a href="#mobile-work">Work</a><a href="#mobile-team">Team</a><a href="#mobile-tech">Tech</a>
                  </div>
                  <div class="phone-section" id="mobile-impact">
                    <div class="phone-label">01 / Impact</div>
                    <div class="phone-cards">
                      <div class="phone-card"><b>Scale</b><span>ML capabilities across Prima’s markets.</span></div>
                      <div class="phone-card"><b>Lifecycle</b><span>From experimentation to production.</span></div>
                      <div class="phone-card"><b>Collaboration</b><span>Product, Data Science and ML Engineering.</span></div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="phone-section" id="mobile-work">
                    <div class="phone-label">02 / Work</div>
                    <p>Four concise workstreams replace long blocks of copy and keep the page scannable with one thumb.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="phone-section" id="mobile-team">
                    <div class="phone-label">03 / Team</div>
                    <div class="phone-pills"><span>Product</span><span>Data Science</span><span>ML Engineering</span><span>Software Engineering</span></div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="phone-section" id="mobile-tech">
                    <div class="phone-label">04 / Tech</div>
                    <div class="phone-pills"><span>Python</span><span>TDD</span><span>CI/CD</span><span>IaC</span><span>Kafka</span></div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="phone-section phone-growth">
                    <div class="phone-label">05 / Growth</div>
                    <p>Learning resources · Mentorship · Personal growth plan</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="mobile-sticky-cta">Apply now ↗</div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="mobile-differences">
                <div class="mobile-difference"><span>01</span><div><b>Sticky apply CTA</b><small>The action stays reachable without forcing the user back to the top.</small></div></div>
                <div class="mobile-difference"><span>02</span><div><b>Compact navigation</b><small>Section links become a horizontally scrollable row instead of a desktop rail.</small></div></div>
                <div class="mobile-difference"><span>03</span><div><b>Stacked information</b><small>Cards and facts collapse vertically so the same content remains readable on a narrow viewport.</small></div></div>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="shell">
          <div class="principle-band">
            <div class="eyebrow">Design principle</div>
            <p>Role → Impact → Work → Team → Technology → Growth → Hiring → EVP</p>
            <span>Desktop is the primary experience. Responsive behaviour preserves the same decision logic while adapting navigation, density and actions to the screen.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="shell footer-grid">
        <div><div class="eyebrow">02 / Task 2</div><p style="margin-top:8px">Make something better</p></div>
        <a class="small" href="/prima-employer-brand-takehome/sources/">Sources & method →</a>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <style is="global">
      /* Brand palette based on the supplied Prima Assicurazioni screenshots */
      .task2-page {
        --prima-purple: #8334c2;
        --prima-purple-dark: #5b2487;
        --prima-navy: #21283a;
        --prima-teal: #00839e;
        --prima-lilac: #efe9ff;
      }

      @media (min-width: 1100px) {
        .task2-page .task-hero .task-head { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 18px; align-items: start; }
        .task2-page .task-hero .task-head > * { justify-self: start; }
        .task2-page .task-hero h1 { max-width: 11ch; }
      }

      .task2-page .job-current-hero,
      .task2-page .after-hero,
      .task2-page .principle-band { background: var(--prima-navy); }

      .task2-page .current-highlight { background: var(--prima-lilac); border-left-color: var(--prima-purple); }
      .task2-page .friction-number,
      .task2-page .task-number::before { background: var(--prima-purple); }
      .task2-page .asset-meta-card span { border-color: #ded4ef; background: #fbf8ff; }
      .task2-page .after-apply,
      .task2-page .current-apply-note,
      .task2-page .rail-card { border-color: rgba(131,52,194,.24); }

      .task2-page .current-apply-note {
        width: auto;
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        align-self: start;
        padding: 11px 16px;
        border: 0;
        border-radius: 10px;
        background: var(--prima-teal);
        color: white;
        text-decoration: none;
        box-shadow: none;
      }
      .task2-page .current-apply-note b { margin: 0; font-size: .76rem; }
      .task2-page .current-apply-note:hover,
      .task2-page .after-apply a:hover,
      .task2-page .rail-apply:hover,
      .task2-page .final-apply a:hover { background: var(--prima-navy); }

      .task2-page .after-apply {
        background: rgba(131,52,194,.08);
      }
      .task2-page .after-apply a,
      .task2-page .rail-apply,
      .task2-page .final-apply a {
        background: var(--prima-teal);
        color: white;
      }
      .task2-page .tech-row span { background: var(--prima-navy); }
      .task2-page .tech-row.optional span { background: white; }
      .task2-page .mobile-sticky-cta {
        background: var(--prima-teal);
        color: white;
      }
      .task2-page .mobile-difference > span { background: var(--prima-lilac); }
      .task2-page .phone-bar { background: var(--prima-navy); }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
